<title>USA: Occidental Petroleum Corp Q3 net rose.</title>
<headline>Occidental Petroleum Corp Q3 net rose.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.53		    $0.36</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$0.50		    $0.36</p>
<p> Net			194,000		  139,000</p>
<p> Revs		   2,786,000		2,557,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 325,300		  318,600</p>
<p>		     Nine Months</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.37		    $1.37</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$1.33		    $1.33</p>
<p> Net			509,000		  504,000</p>
<p> Revs		   7,765,000		7,950,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 322,400		  318,000</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call consensus Q3 estimate was $0.43/shr.</p>
<p>1996 Q3 net includes $100 million benefit from reduced federal tax liabilities and $105 million charge to write-down Russian oil and natural gas investment.</p>
<p>1996 nine months also includes extraordinary loss of $30 million, equal to $0.05/shr primary, $0.04/shr diluted.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
